Library ( Opens in new tab ) Svenska sv Search Menu Education Research Collaborate with us About Chalmers Current Departments Assistant professor positions Home About Chalmers Work with us Assistant professor positions Turn your vision into progress Image 1 of 1 Chalmers is now looking for 11 creative individuals with visionary ideas in energy, nanoscience, materials science, production, transportation, new space, mechanical engineering, batteries and basic sciences. Are you one of them? Content on this page Brief timeline The offer Explore all positions Meet some of your forerunners A great university A great place to live Application closed The application for the seventh global recruitment round for Assistant Professors is now closed. Please see timeline below for information about the  process. Brief timeline March – May May – August August –September Mid-September – Mid-October October Applications period 27 March - 1 May Selections, internal and external review Invitations to interviews Interviews Position offer to candidates Starting date is flexible but not later than first half of 2027. The offer Great science starts with the freedom to think and explore. As an Assistant Professor at Chalmers, you can turn your scientific curiosity into ideas, your ideas into experiments, and your experiments into discoveries. The position is a five-year tenure-track appointment with a competitive start-up package including funding for personnel, equipment, and operational costs.You will also get relocation support, mentoring, and leadership training to support your development as an independent research leader and educator. The position also includes the same generous benefits and conditions that come with all Chalmers positions. As an Assistant Professor at Chalmers, you are invited to unleash your visionary ideas and push the boundaries of knowledge. Martin Nilsson Jacobi President and CEO of Chalmers University of Technology Explore all positions At Chalmers, we are committed to improve diversity in our faculty, and we encourage applications from individuals of all genders, backgrounds, and identities. The applications closes May 1. The applications will be reviewed during March – June, and interviews are planned for September – October 2026. The offered positions Basic Science Batteries Energy Materials Science Mechanical Engineering Nanoscience New Space Production Transport Meet some of your forerunners The position as an Assistant Professor is the first step in your academic journey. From here, there are many ways to progress. This is a position where your skills grow, your curiosity deepens and your future in science takes shape. Want to know more? Hear from the people who’ve made the journey before you. Image 1 of 1 Watch the video to learn why Shantanu Mishra decided to join Chalmers as an Assistant Professor Image 1 of 1 Watch the video to learn why Angela Grommet and Arion Pons decided to join Chalmers as Assistant Professors Image 1 of 1 Watch the video to learn why Mélanie Despeisse and Giuseppe Durisi decided to join Chalmers as Assistant Professors Image 1 of 1 Watch the video to learn why Jessica Jewell decided to join Chalmers as an Assistant Professor A great university Chalmers University of Technology is one of the leading technical universities in the Nordic region, with a strong reputation for applied research, close collaboration with industry and a clear focus on sustainability. Chalmers’ vision is to become a world-leading technical university. We aim to take greater responsibility for societal development – through education, research, and innovation. Our vision is founded on the belief that knowledge changes the world. Research infrastructures To reach a breakthrough, you need the right conditions. Here, you get access to world-class labs and the infrastructure needed to push the boundaries of your field. Entrepreneurship and innovation Breakthroughs are rarely made alone. Through our entrepreneurial ecosystem, you get the support you need to bring research and technology ideas to market. Reputation and ranking Chalmers University of Technology is one of the leading technical universities in the Nordic region, with a strong reputation for applied research, close collaboration with industry and a clear focus on sustainability.\nIn national surveys, Chalmers is consistently rated as the best known and most highly trusted university in Sweden and gets top scores on learning by students in the International Students Barometer. A culture of well-being People need to be well in order to be creative. Sweden is renowned for its high quality of life, and at Chalmers, this is part of our DNA. A great place to live ​On the west coast of Sweden, Gothenburg is a perfectly sized ‘big little city’, with a population of around 570,000. Chalmers’ campus is right in the heart of Gothenburg making the university well embedded into the life of the city. The friendly, welcoming attitude here will ensure you quickly feel at home – Gothenburg has previously been voted ‘the world’s most sociable city’. And the locals speak excellent English, so everyday life is usually pretty straightforward here. Living in Sweden Sweden is world-famous for its beautiful and clean nature, its modern and digital society, and its relaxed and tolerant way of life. Here, it’s easy for you and your family to make yourself a rich and comfortable life. ( Opens in new tab ) Move to Gothenburg Gothenburg is situated on the Swedish west coast with a beautiful archipelago and lush, green forests next door. It’s a contemporary and outgoing city, known for its friendly atmosphere and international vibe. ( Opens in new tab ) Updated 2 June 2026, 13:41 Published 19 March 2026, 09:50 Assistant professor positions Basic Science Batteries Energy Materials Science Mechanical Engineering Nanoscience New Space Production Transport Related content Reputation and ranking Our vision: World in progress Research infrastructures Research areas Departments Contact Chalmers Phone +46-317721000 Mail address Chalmers University of Technology 412 96 Gothenburg E-mail and more contact information Organisation number 556479-5598 Education Education Your studies Our Master's degree programmes Student support Services and tools Canvas learning management system Safe at Chalmers Chalmers student union Shortcuts Shortcuts Work at Chalmers Press and media Whistleblowing at Chalmers Safety and emergency situations Supplier information Chalmers University of Technology Foundation About the website About the website Cookies Processing of personal data Accessibility statement Service Disruptions at Chalmers Contact Chalmers Phone +46-317721000 Mail address Chalmers University of Technology 412 96 Gothenburg E-mail and more contact information Organisation number 556479-5598 Social media Instagram ( Opens in new tab ) Tiktok ( Opens in new tab ) Youtube ( Opens in new tab ) LinkedIn ( Opens in new tab ) Facebook ( Opens in new tab ) With scientific excellence as a basis, Chalmers conducts research and education in technology, natural sciences, maritime studies and architecture. Social media Instagram ( Opens in new tab ) Tiktok ( Opens in new tab ) Youtube ( Opens in new tab ) LinkedIn ( Opens in new tab ) Facebook ( Opens in new tab )"
