esearch Collaborate with us About Chalmers Current Departments Assistant professor positions Home About Chalmers Work with us Assistant professor positions Basic Science Available position: Assistant Professor in Basic Science Image 1 of 1 Chalmers now seeks curious and creative individuals for tenure-track Assistant Professors. As an Assistant Professor in Basic Science at Chalmers, you can turn your scientific curiosity into ideas, your ideas into experiments, and your experiments into discoveries. Application closed The application for the seventh global recruitment round for Assistant Professors is now closed. Basic Science: Pushing the boundaries of knowledge Basic Science at Chalmers addresses fundamental questions in mathematics, physics, astronomy, chemistry, material science and the life sciences. Our research spans areas such as mathematical modelling, complex systems, quantum science, fundamental chemistry and physics, biomolecular systems and nanoscale phenomena. Driven by curiosity, we combine theoretical, experimental and computational approaches to advance fundamental understanding and explore new scientific frontiers. Chalmers offers a collaborative and international research environment with strong interdisciplinary connections. The position is a five-year tenure-track appointment with a competitive start-up package including funding for personnel, equipment, and operational costs.You will also get relocation support, mentoring, and leadership training to support your development as an independent research leader and educator. The research spans several departments, including but not limited to: Chemistry and Chemical Engineering Life Sciences Mathematical Sciences Microtechnology and Nanoscience Physics and Astronomy Linked research infrastructures Chalmers e-Commons Chalmers Materials Analysis Laboratory (CMAL) Nanofabrication Laboratory (Myfab) National Academic Infrastructure for Super­computing in Sweden (NAISS) Onsala Space Observatory SciLife