 in new tab ) Library ( Opens in new tab ) Svenska sv Search Menu Education Research Collaborate with us About Chalmers Current Departments Assistant professor positions Home About Chalmers Work with us Assistant professor positions Mechanical Engineering Available position: Assistant Professor in Mechanical Engineering Image 1 of 1 Chalmers now seeks curious and creative individuals for tenure-track Assistant Professors. As an Assistant Professor in Mechanical Engineering at Chalmers, you can turn your scientific curiosity into ideas, your ideas into experiments, and your experiments into discoveries. Application closed The application for the seventh global recruitment round for Assistant Professors is now closed. Advancing engineering for a sustainable and competitive industry Mechanical engineering at Chalmers brings together expertise in mechanics, materials, manufacturing, vehicle engineering and product development to address major industrial and societal challenges. By combining fundamental engineering science with digital technologies, modelling and experimentation, we develop new solutions for sustainable transport systems, advanced manufacturing and next-generation engineering design. Close collaboration with industry and strong research infrastructure make Chalmers an attractive environment for innovation in mechanical engineering. The position is a five-year tenure-track appointment with a competitive start-up package including funding for personnel, equipment, and operational costs.You will also get relocation support, mentoring, and leadership training to support your development as an independent research leader and educator. The research spans several of Chalmers departments, including but not limited to the department of Mechanical Engineering . Linked research infrastructures and centres Chalmers Materials Analysis Laboratory (CMAL) SAFER – Vehicle and traffic safety centre Stena Industry Innovation Laboratory for industrial production system Wingquist Laboratory Learn more about the offer Brief timeline, available positions and more information about the offer For questions about the process, please contact Recruitment systems support HR department, Chalmers operations support Contact rekr.stodet@chalmers.se For questions about the position, please contact To personal page Rikard Söderberg Head of Department , Mechanical Engineering Contact rikard.soderberg@chalmers.se +46 31 772 86 17 To personal page Updated 2 June 2026, 13:44 Published 20 March 2026, 09:00 Leave feedback Assistant professor positions Basic Science Batteries Energy Materials Science Mechanical Engineering Nanoscience New Space Production Transport Related content Reputation and ranking Our vision: World in progress Research infrastructures Research areas Departments For questions about the process, please contact Recruitment systems support HR department, Chalmers operations support Contact rekr.stodet@chalmers.se For questions about the position, please contact To personal page Rikard Söderberg Head of Department , Mechanical Engineering Contact rikard.soderberg@chalmers.se +46 31 772 86 17 To personal page You may also be interested in Available position: Assistant Professor in Materials Science Available position: Assistant Professor in Transport Available position: Assistant Professor in Production Available position: Assistant Professor in Nanoscience Contact Chalmers Phone +46-317721000 Mail address Chalmers University of Technology 412 96 Gothenburg E-mail and more contact information Organisation number 556479-5598 Education Education Your studies Our Master's degree programmes Student support Services and tools Canvas learning management system Safe at Chalmers Chalmers student union Shortcuts Shortcuts Work at Chalmers Press and media Whistleblowing at Chalmers Safety and emergency situations Supplier information Chalmers University of Technology Foundation About the website About the website Cookies Processing of personal data 