esearch Collaborate with us About Chalmers Current Departments Assistant professor positions Home About Chalmers Work with us Assistant professor positions Production Available position: Assistant Professor in Production Image 1 of 1 Chalmers now seeks curious and creative individuals for tenure-track Assistant Professors. As an Assistant Professor in Production at Chalmers, you can turn your scientific curiosity into ideas, your ideas into experiments, and your experiments into discoveries. Application closed The application for the seventh global recruitment round for Assistant Professors is now closed. Advancing sustainable industrial innovation Chalmers has a strong and forward-looking position in the broad area of Production, with a cross-disciplinary focus on digitalised production systems, scalable and robust manufacturing processes, digital product and process development, and production within a circular economy. Research is carried out in close collaboration with industry and research institutes in Sweden and internationally. By combining engineering science, digital technologies and industrial applications, we develop new methods and tools to transform current practice and develop new solutions for the next generation of sustainable and competitive manufacturing systems. The position as Assistant Professor comes with a five-year tenure track position with a generous start-up package, relocation support and mentoring, and leadership training to further your development as research leader and teacher. The research spans several departments, including but not limited to: Chemistry and Chemical Engineering Computer Science and Engineering Electrical Engineering Environmental and Energy Sciences Mechanical Engineering Microtechnology and Nanoscience Technology Management and Economics Linked research infrastructures and centres: Centre for Process Engineering (CPE) Competence Centre Recycling (CCR) MAXBATT Competence Centre Metal Cutting Research Centre (MCR) Stena Industry Innovation Laboratory Swedish Life Cycle Centre (SLC) Vinnova Competence Centre for Additive Manufacturing – Metals (CAM2) Wingquist Laboratory Learn more about the offer Brief timeline, available positions and more information about the offer For questions about the process, please contact Recruitment systems support HR department, Chalmers operations support Contact rekr.stodet@chalmers.se For questions about the position, please contact To personal page Árni Halldórsson Styrkeområdesledare , Supply and Operations Management, Technology Management and Economics Contact arni.halldorsson@chalmers.se +46 31 772 15 82 To personal page Updated 2 June 2026, 13:45 Published 12 December 2023, 17:10 Assistant professor positions Basic Science Batteries Energy Materials Science Mechanical Engineering Nanoscience New Space Production Transport Related content Reputation and ranking Our vision: World in progress Research infrastructures Research areas Departments For questions about the process, please contact Recruitment systems support HR department, Chalmers operations support Contact rekr.stodet@chalmers.se For questions about the position, please contact To personal page Árni Halldórsson Styrkeområdesledare , Supply and Operations Management, Technology Management and Economics Contact arni.halldorsson@chalmers.se +46 31 772 15 82 To personal page Contact Chalmers Phone +46-317721000 Mail address Chalmers University of Technology 412 96 Gothenburg E-mail and more contact information Organisation number 556479-5598 Education Education Your studies Our Master's degree programmes Student support Services and tools Canvas learning management system Safe at Chalmers Chalmers student union Shortcuts Shortcuts Work at Chalmers Press and media Whistleblowing at Chalmers Safety and emergency situations Supplier information Chalmers University of Technology Foundation About the website About the website Cookies Processing of personal data Accessibility statement Ser